		<div id="v95n2o">
			<div class="RelativePositionComponent WhiteBackgroundComponent">
				<div class="AutoHorizontalMarginComponent MaxWidthSevenXLComponent LargeGridComponent LargeGridTwelveColumnsComponent LargeHorizontalGapEightComponent LargeHorizontalPaddingEightComponent">
					<div class="HorizontalPaddingSixComponent BottomPaddingTwentyFourComponent TopPaddingTenComponent SmallBottomPaddingThirtyTwoComponent LargeColSpanSevenComponent LargeHorizontalPaddingZeroComponent LargeBottomPaddingFiftySixComponent LargeTopPaddingFortyEightComponent ExtraLargeColSpanSixComponent">
						<div class="AutoHorizontalMarginComponent MaxWidthTwoXLComponent LargeAutoHorizontalMarginZeroComponent">
							<h1 class="TopMarginTwentyFourComponent TextFourXLComponent BoldFontComponent TightTrackingComponent GrayTextNineHundredComponent SmallTopMarginTenComponent SmallTextSixXLComponent">Interior Design Shaped Around the Way You Live</h1>
							<p class="TopMarginSixComponent LargeTextComponent LeadingEightComponent GrayTextSixHundredComponent">
								Flourish Room Design explores considered interior design for homes across England, balancing personal style with the practical needs of everyday life. A project can begin with a single room, a layout challenge or a broader vision for a home. The design process may bring together space planning, colour direction, material choices, lighting ideas and furniture suggestions, always in response to the brief rather than a one-size-fits-all look. Whether you are gathering early
								inspiration or ready to discuss a specific space, start with what matters most to you: how the room should feel, what it needs to do and which details make it yours. Scope, timing and availability can be discussed before any work is agreed.
							</p>
							<div class="TopMarginTenComponent FlexDisplayComponent CenteredItemsComponent HorizontalGapSixComponent">
								<a href="#" class="LargeRoundedComponent bg--600 HorizontalPaddingSixComponent VerticalPaddingFourComponent LargeTextComponent SemiBoldFontComponent WhiteTextComponent SmallShadowComponent hover:bg--500 FocusVisibleOutlineComponent FocusVisibleOutlineTwoComponent FocusVisibleOutlineOffsetTwoComponent focus-visible:outline--600"></a>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="RelativePositionComponent LargeColSpanFiveComponent LargeNegativeRightMarginEightComponent ExtraLargeAbsolutePositionComponent ExtraLargeInsetZeroComponent ExtraLargeLeftHalfPositionComponent ExtraLargeRightZeroMarginComponent">
						<img class="AspectRatioThreeByTwoComponent FullWidthComponent GrayBackgroundFiftyComponent CoverObjectComponent LargeAbsolutePositionComponent LargeInsetZeroComponent LargeAspectAutoComponent LargeFullHeightComponent" src="img/5741c65e9380d01ffc788efe53378f74.jpg" alt="" />
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div id="im179">
			<section class="GrayTextTwoHundredComponent body-font EmeraldBackgroundHundredComponent">
				<div class="ContainerComponent HorizontalPaddingFiveComponent VerticalPaddingTwentyFourComponent AutoHorizontalMarginComponent FlexDisplayComponent FlexWrapComponent">
					<div class="FlexDisplayComponent FlexColumnComponent CenterAlignedTextComponent FullWidthComponent BottomMarginTwentyComponent">
						<h1 class="SmallTextFourXLComponent TextThreeXLComponent BoldFontComponent title-font YellowTextFiveHundredComponent">A Thoughtful Approach to Every Room</h1>
						<p class="LargeTwoThirdsWidthComponent AutoHorizontalMarginComponent RelaxedLeadingComponent BaseTextComponent GrayTextNineHundredComponent">
							Good interior design is more than selecting attractive finishes. It considers how people move through a space, what they need to store, how natural and artificial light affect the room, and which materials feel right for daily use. Flourish Room Design takes these connected elements into account when developing ideas for homes in England. The aim is to create a clear design direction that reflects your brief, respects the character of the property and helps you make informed
							choices. Every project has its own requirements, so the proposed scope and next steps are discussed with you rather than assumed.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="LargeTwoThirdsWidthComponent AutoHorizontalMarginComponent">
						<div class="FlexDisplayComponent FlexWrapComponent NegativeMarginFourComponent">
							<div class="PaddingFourComponent LargeHalfWidthComponent MediumFullWidthComponent">
								<div class="FlexDisplayComponent TwoBorderComponent GrayBorderSevenHundredComponent LargeRoundedComponent PaddingEightComponent FlexColumnComponent GrayBackgroundSixHundredComponent">
									<h2 class="TextXLComponent MediumFontComponent YellowTextFiveHundredComponent BottomMarginTwoComponent">Design Led by Your Brief</h2>
									<p class="LargeTextComponent RelaxedLeadingComponent GrayTextThreeHundredComponent">
										A useful design starts with listening. Share what is working, what feels difficult and what you would like to change, along with any practical requirements such as storage, circulation or flexible use. Your preferences, existing furniture and the character of the property can all help shape the direction. Rather than applying a fixed style to every home, Flourish Room Design can use the brief to guide decisions about layout, colour, materials and furnishings. This keeps the
										conversation grounded in your priorities and gives you a clearer basis for reviewing ideas.
									</p>
								</div>
							</div>
							<div class="PaddingFourComponent LargeHalfWidthComponent MediumFullWidthComponent">
								<div class="FlexDisplayComponent TwoBorderComponent GrayBorderSevenHundredComponent LargeRoundedComponent PaddingEightComponent FlexColumnComponent GrayBackgroundSixHundredComponent">
									<h2 class="TextXLComponent MediumFontComponent YellowTextFiveHundredComponent BottomMarginTwoComponent">Connected Room Planning</h2>
									<p class="LargeTextComponent RelaxedLeadingComponent GrayTextThreeHundredComponent">
										Layout decisions influence how a room feels and functions, so they deserve attention alongside colour and decoration. Considering routes through the space, furniture proportions, useful zones and storage can help reveal opportunities before individual pieces are selected. Flourish Room Design considers these relationships as part of a joined-up interior concept, with suggestions shaped by the room and its intended use. The goal is not to promise a particular outcome, but to
										make the choices easier to understand and discuss. Any measurements, constraints or technical requirements should be checked for the specific property.
									</p>
								</div>
							</div>
							<div class="PaddingFourComponent LargeHalfWidthComponent MediumFullWidthComponent TopMarginFourComponent">
								<div class="FlexDisplayComponent TwoBorderComponent GrayBorderSevenHundredComponent LargeRoundedComponent PaddingEightComponent FlexColumnComponent GrayBackgroundSixHundredComponent">
									<h2 class="TextXLComponent MediumFontComponent YellowTextFiveHundredComponent BottomMarginTwoComponent">Colour and Material Clarity</h2>
									<p class="LargeTextComponent RelaxedLeadingComponent GrayTextThreeHundredComponent">
										Choosing finishes can feel complicated when colours, textures and surfaces are considered in isolation. A considered palette looks at how elements relate to one another, how daylight and room orientation may affect their appearance, and how the space is intended to be used. Flourish Room Design can help organise these decisions into a coherent direction, drawing on your preferences and the character of the home. Product availability, suitability and care requirements should
										be confirmed with the relevant supplier or professional before purchase. The emphasis is on informed selection, not unsupported claims about performance.
									</p>
								</div>
							</div>
							<div class="PaddingFourComponent LargeHalfWidthComponent MediumFullWidthComponent TopMarginFourComponent">
								<div class="FlexDisplayComponent TwoBorderComponent GrayBorderSevenHundredComponent LargeRoundedComponent PaddingEightComponent FlexColumnComponent GrayBackgroundSixHundredComponent">
									<h2 class="TextXLComponent MediumFontComponent YellowTextFiveHundredComponent BottomMarginTwoComponent">Practical, Personal Details</h2>
									<p class="LargeTextComponent RelaxedLeadingComponent GrayTextThreeHundredComponent">
										A room should reflect the people who use it, as well as support the routines that take place there. Details such as lighting layers, storage, furniture scale and the placement of everyday items can influence comfort and usability. Flourish Room Design considers these practical needs alongside the visual direction, so design discussions can address both appearance and function. The right balance depends on the project, budget and property, and no single solution suits every
										home. You can discuss which details matter most and clarify what is included before deciding how to proceed.
									</p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</div>
