		<div id="a8vh">
			<div class="WhiteBackgroundComponent VerticalBorderComponent">
				<div class="AutoHorizontalMarginComponent MaxWidthSevenXLComponent HorizontalPaddingSixComponent VerticalPaddingSixteenComponent SmallVerticalPaddingTwentyFourComponent LargeHorizontalPaddingEightComponent">
					<div class="AutoHorizontalMarginComponent MaxWidthTwoXLComponent CenterAlignedTextComponent">
						<h2 class="TextTwoXLComponent BoldFontComponent LeadingTenComponent TightTrackingComponent GrayTextNineHundredComponent">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
						<p class="TopMarginSixComponent BaseTextComponent LeadingSevenComponent GrayTextSixHundredComponent">Every interior project has its own context, from the size and character of the property to the decisions you would like help exploring. These answers offer a starting point for understanding the design approach. Please confirm the available services, project scope, timing and any fees directly with Flourish Room Design before making plans.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="TopMarginTwentyComponent">
						<dl class="VerticalSpaceSixteenComponent SmallGridComponent SmallGridTwoColumnsComponent SmallHorizontalGapSixComponent SmallVerticalGapSixteenComponent SmallVerticalSpaceZeroComponent LargeHorizontalGapTenComponent">
							<div>
								<dt class="BaseTextComponent SemiBoldFontComponent LeadingSevenComponent GrayTextNineHundredComponent">What kinds of interior design projects can I discuss?</dt>
								<dd class="TopMarginTwoComponent BaseTextComponent LeadingSevenComponent GrayTextSixHundredComponent">You can enquire about a home interior project, whether you are thinking about one room or a broader design direction. Share the space, your aims and the decisions you would like help with. The studio can then clarify whether the request fits its current services and discuss an appropriate scope.</dd>
							</div>
							<div>
								<dt class="BaseTextComponent SemiBoldFontComponent LeadingSevenComponent GrayTextNineHundredComponent">Do I need a finished brief before getting in touch?</dt>
								<dd class="TopMarginTwoComponent BaseTextComponent LeadingSevenComponent GrayTextSixHundredComponent">No finished brief is needed to begin a conversation. It can be helpful to describe what is not working, how you use the room and what you hope to change. Images, measurements and inspiration can be useful later, but any specific information needed will depend on the project and should be discussed directly.</dd>
							</div>
							<div>
								<dt class="BaseTextComponent SemiBoldFontComponent LeadingSevenComponent GrayTextNineHundredComponent">Can you work with the furniture and finishes I already have?</dt>
								<dd class="TopMarginTwoComponent BaseTextComponent LeadingSevenComponent GrayTextSixHundredComponent">Existing furniture, artwork or finishes can be part of the design discussion. Tell the studio which items you would like to keep and any practical constraints that matter to you. Whether an item can be incorporated depends on the room, the design brief and the details of the project.</dd>
							</div>
							<div>
								<dt class="BaseTextComponent SemiBoldFontComponent LeadingSevenComponent GrayTextNineHundredComponent">Do you provide a fixed price or project timeline?</dt>
								<dd class="TopMarginTwoComponent BaseTextComponent LeadingSevenComponent GrayTextSixHundredComponent">Fees and timing depend on the project scope and should be confirmed directly before work is agreed. Describe the rooms, support you are seeking and any relevant deadlines so the studio can explain what may be possible. No price, availability or completion date is implied by this website copy.</dd>
							</div>
						</dl>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
